# Amendment #133 — Dev-pattern simplifications #1

2026-05-04. Per
`docs/rebuild/plans/dev-pattern-simplifications-1.md` and
cost-audit at
`docs/rebuild/plans/cost-audit-loam-dev-pattern-2026-05-04.md`
Recommendations A, D, E.

Three simplifications landed together inside the dev-sdlc fence:

- **A — Manifest narrative collapse.** New schema v3 introduces
  an optional top-level `plan_doc_ref:` field. `narrative.body`
  becomes optional at v3. When v3 manifest carries
  `plan_doc_ref` only, the seal step synthesizes a 5-15 line
  summary instead of inlining ~150 LOC of duplicated narrative
  per amendment.

- **D — Manifest+apply commit merge.** Schema v3 `loam amend
  apply` stages the manifest YAML alongside BASELINE/sidecar
  bumps and produces ONE commit (subject token: `manifest+apply`)
  instead of two. Schema v1/v2 preserve the legacy two-commit
  ladder verbatim.

- **E — Amendment-number deprecation.** Schema v3 makes
  `amendment.number` optional; identification is by `slug` only.
  Apply/seal commit subjects degrade gracefully when number is
  None (no `#N` prefix). v1/v2 still require number.

